<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19677" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glōrĭātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				glorying</i>, <i>boasting</i>, <i>vaunting</i>, <i>exulting</i> (a word formed by
			Cic.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex quo efficitur, gloriatione, ut ita dicam,
					dignam esse beatam vitam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 3, 8, 28</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 18, 50</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubi est ergo gloriatio tua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Rom. 3, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
